central-ui/node_modules
central-ui/dist
# Dockerfile.gateway needs the built SPA in its build context -- everything
# else (Dockerfile.central, which only needs central-ui's separately-built
# "forms" under central/src/main/resources, not dist/) never references
# this path, so un-excluding it here doesn't change what those get.
#
# Both lines needed: the first re-includes the dist/ directory entry
# itself, the second explicitly re-includes everything under it. Verified
# by hand (a full local build + running the resulting versola-gateway
# image, with central-ui's admin console loading and working end-to-end)
# that this isn't Docker's documented "can't re-include a file under an
# excluded parent" trap -- that applies to re-including a *child* while
# the parent stays excluded, not re-including the same path that was
# excluded. Both lines are here anyway so the intent doesn't rely on that
# distinction being obvious to the next person reading this file.
!central-ui/dist
!central-ui/dist/**
